architecture-beta
accTitle: Industrial machine connectivity - reconstruction of the AWS reference
accDescr: EOT Twin Talk sends time-series data directly to SiteWise and asset metadata through S3, Lambda and DynamoDB. SiteWise updates flow through IoT Core and Firehose to an industrial data lake. Reconstruction, not an AWS-authored diagram.
%% Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/reference-architecture-diagrams/latest/industrial-machine-connectivity-eot/industrial-machine-connectivity-eot.html
%% The original diagram, not only its prose, distinguishes metadata from time-series ingestion.
group industrial(cloud)[Industrial refineries and wells]
group historians(server)[Supported historians and SCADA] in industrial
group edge(server)[Industrial PC] in industrial
group aws(cloud)[AWS Cloud]
group amc(server)[Asset Model Converter - AMC] in aws
service sensors(lucide:radio-tower)[Devices and sensors] in industrial
service pi(server)[OSIsoft PI] in historians
service cygnet(server)[CygNet OPC and SCADA] in historians
service legacy(database)[Legacy historians] in historians
service twin(server)[EOT Twin Talk Express] in edge
service incoming(aws:s3)[AMC incoming bucket] in amc
service convert(aws:lambda)[AMC1 normalize model] in amc
service definitions(aws:dynamodb)[Asset model definitions] in amc
service create(aws:lambda)[AMC2 create assets] in amc
service sitewise(lucide:factory)[AWS IoT SiteWise] in aws
service core(lucide:network)[AWS IoT Core rule] in aws
service firehose(lucide:workflow)[Amazon Data Firehose] in aws
service lake(aws:s3)[Industrial data lake] in aws
%% Steps 1-2: collector protocols and multiplicity are aggregated, not deployment instructions.
sensors:R --> L:pi
sensors:B --> B:cygnet
sensors:B --> B:legacy
pi:B --> R:twin
cygnet:B --> B:twin
legacy:B --> B:twin
%% Independent paths shown in the original: time series direct to SiteWise, metadata via AMC.
twin:L -[Time series]-> R:sitewise
twin:B -[Asset metadata]-> L:incoming
incoming:R --> L:convert
convert:R --> L:definitions
definitions:R -[DynamoDB Streams]-> L:create
create:T --> B:sitewise
sitewise:T -[Property updates]-> B:core
core:R --> L:firehose
firehose:R --> L:lake
%% ML and third-party consumers are described in step 10 but are not drawn in the original.
